Now I have a complete picture of the existing project. It is a clean Next.js 16.1.6 starter with React 19.2.3, Tailwind CSS v4 (using `@import "tailwindcss"` and `@theme inline`), Geist fonts, and no custom components. Let me now design the full implementation plan.

---

# Polyglot -- Language Learning App Implementation Plan

## 1. Project Structure

The following directory tree shows every new file to create under `src/`. The existing files (`src/app/layout.tsx`, `src/app/page.tsx`, `src/app/globals.css`) will be modified in place.

```
src/
  types/
    index.ts                    # All shared TypeScript interfaces/types
  lib/
    storage/
      interface.ts              # StorageProvider interface (the abstraction layer)
      local-storage.ts          # localStorage implementation of StorageProvider
      index.ts                  # Re-export, factory function
    sm2.ts                      # SM-2 spaced repetition algorithm
    utils.ts                    # General helpers (ID generation, date formatting)
  data/
    languages.ts                # Language registry (metadata for each language)
    japanese/
      vocabulary.ts             # Japanese vocabulary entries
      lessons.ts                # Japanese lesson definitions
      quizzes.ts                # Japanese quiz definitions
    spanish/
      vocabulary.ts
      lessons.ts
      quizzes.ts
    french/
      vocabulary.ts
      lessons.ts
      quizzes.ts
  contexts/
    app-context.tsx             # AppProvider: selected language, user profile
    flashcard-context.tsx       # Flashcard state + SM-2 scheduling
  components/
    layout/
      app-shell.tsx             # Sidebar/nav + main content area (client component)
      sidebar.tsx               # Navigation sidebar
      mobile-nav.tsx            # Bottom tab bar for mobile
    ui/
      button.tsx                # Reusable button
      card.tsx                  # Reusable card container
      progress-bar.tsx          # Progress bar component
      badge.tsx                 # Status badges (mastery level, score)
      modal.tsx                 # Modal/dialog
    dashboard/
      dashboard-page.tsx        # Dashboard overview
      language-selector.tsx     # Language picker (onboarding + settings)
      progress-summary.tsx      # Per-language progress stats
    flashcards/
      flashcard-page.tsx        # Main flashcard study view
      flashcard.tsx             # Single card (flip animation)
      flashcard-controls.tsx    # Rating buttons (Again/Hard/Good/Easy)
      flashcard-stats.tsx       # Session stats (cards due, mastered, etc.)
    lessons/
      lessons-list-page.tsx     # Browse lessons for current language
      lesson-detail-page.tsx    # Single lesson content view
      lesson-card.tsx           # Lesson preview card in the list
      vocabulary-table.tsx      # Vocabulary introduced in a lesson
      grammar-block.tsx         # Grammar explanation block
    quizzes/
      quiz-page.tsx             # Quiz session view
      quiz-question.tsx         # Single question renderer
      multiple-choice.tsx       # Multiple choice question type
      fill-in-blank.tsx         # Fill-in-the-blank question type
      translation.tsx           # Translation exercise question type
      quiz-results.tsx          # Score summary after quiz
    conversation/
      conversation-page.tsx     # AI conversation practice
      message-bubble.tsx        # Chat message bubble
      conversation-input.tsx    # Text input for conversation
  app/
    layout.tsx                  # (MODIFY) Wrap with providers, add AppShell
    page.tsx                    # (MODIFY) Redirect to /dashboard or /onboarding
    globals.css                 # (MODIFY) Add custom theme tokens, component styles
    dashboard/
      page.tsx                  # Dashboard route
    flashcards/
      page.tsx                  # Flashcard study route
    lessons/
      page.tsx                  # Lessons list route
      [lessonId]/
        page.tsx                # Individual lesson route
    quizzes/
      [quizId]/
        page.tsx                # Individual quiz route
    conversation/
      page.tsx                  # AI conversation route
    onboarding/
      page.tsx                  # Language selection (first use)
    api/
      conversation/
        route.ts                # POST endpoint for AI conversation
```

## 2. Key TypeScript Interfaces

All types go in `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/types/index.ts`:

```typescript
// ============================================================
// LANGUAGE & CONTENT DATA TYPES
// ============================================================

export type LanguageCode = "ja" | "es" | "fr";

export interface Language {
  code: LanguageCode;
  name: string;           // "Japanese"
  nativeName: string;     // "日本語"
  flag: string;           // Emoji flag "🇯🇵"
}

export interface VocabularyEntry {
  id: string;                // e.g., "ja-vocab-001"
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  term: string;              // Word in target language
  reading?: string;          // Pronunciation aid (e.g., hiragana for Japanese)
  definition: string;        // English translation
  exampleSentence?: string;  // Example usage
  audioHint?: string;        // Phonetic pronunciation hint
  tags: string[];            // e.g., ["greetings", "N5"]
}

export interface GrammarConcept {
  title: string;
  explanation: string;
  examples: { target: string; english: string }[];
}

export interface Lesson {
  id: string;                // e.g., "ja-lesson-001"
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  order: number;             // Controls sequential progression
  vocabularyIds: string[];   // References to VocabularyEntry.id
  grammar: GrammarConcept[];
  quizId?: string;           // Optional linked quiz
}

export type QuestionType = "multiple-choice" | "fill-in-blank" | "translation";

export interface QuizQuestion {
  id: string;
  type: QuestionType;
  prompt: string;
  // For multiple-choice:
  options?: string[];
  correctAnswer: string;
  // For fill-in-blank:
  sentenceTemplate?: string; // "I ___ a student" (blank replaced)
}

export interface Quiz {
  id: string;               // e.g., "ja-quiz-001"
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  lessonId: string;          // Tied to a lesson
  title: string;
  questions: QuizQuestion[];
}

// ============================================================
// USER PROGRESS & STATE TYPES
// ============================================================

export interface UserProfile {
  id: string;
  selectedLanguage: LanguageCode;
  createdAt: string;  // ISO date
}

// SM-2 algorithm state per flashcard
export interface FlashcardProgress {
  vocabularyId: string;
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  easeFactor: number;     // Starts at 2.5
  interval: number;       // Days until next review
  repetitions: number;    // Number of successful reviews
  nextReviewDate: string; // ISO date
  lastReviewDate: string; // ISO date
}

export type SM2Rating = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5;
// 0 = complete blackout
// 1 = incorrect, but remembered upon seeing answer
// 2 = incorrect, but easy recall after seeing answer
// 3 = correct with serious difficulty
// 4 = correct with hesitation
// 5 = perfect response

export interface LessonProgress {
  lessonId: string;
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  completed: boolean;
  completedAt?: string;  // ISO date
}

export interface QuizAttempt {
  quizId: string;
  languageCode: LanguageCode;
  score: number;         // 0-100
  totalQuestions: number;
  correctAnswers: number;
  attemptedAt: string;   // ISO date
}

export interface ConversationMessage {
  role: "user" | "assistant";
  content: string;
  timestamp: string;
}

// Aggregated user data (what gets persisted)
export interface UserData {
  profile: UserProfile;
  flashcardProgress: Record<string, FlashcardProgress>; // keyed by vocabularyId
  lessonProgress: Record<string, LessonProgress>;        // keyed by lessonId
  quizAttempts: QuizAttempt[];
  conversationHistory: Record<LanguageCode, ConversationMessage[]>;
}
```

## 3. Storage Abstraction Layer

The storage interface in `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/lib/storage/interface.ts`:

```typescript
import type { UserData, FlashcardProgress, LessonProgress, QuizAttempt, UserProfile, ConversationMessage, LanguageCode } from "@/types";

export interface StorageProvider {
  // Profile
  getProfile(): Promise<UserProfile | null>;
  saveProfile(profile: UserProfile): Promise<void>;

  // Flashcard progress
  getFlashcardProgress(vocabularyId: string): Promise<FlashcardProgress | null>;
  getAllFlashcardProgress(languageCode: LanguageCode): Promise<FlashcardProgress[]>;
  saveFlashcardProgress(progress: FlashcardProgress): Promise<void>;

  // Lesson progress
  getLessonProgress(lessonId: string): Promise<LessonProgress | null>;
  getAllLessonProgress(languageCode: LanguageCode): Promise<LessonProgress[]>;
  saveLessonProgress(progress: LessonProgress): Promise<void>;

  // Quiz attempts
  getQuizAttempts(quizId: string): Promise<QuizAttempt[]>;
  saveQuizAttempt(attempt: QuizAttempt): Promise<void>;

  // Conversation
  getConversationHistory(languageCode: LanguageCode): Promise<ConversationMessage[]>;
  saveConversationHistory(languageCode: LanguageCode, messages: ConversationMessage[]): Promise<void>;

  // Bulk operations
  exportAllData(): Promise<UserData>;
  importAllData(data: UserData): Promise<void>;
  clearAllData(): Promise<void>;
}
```

The localStorage implementation in `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/lib/storage/local-storage.ts` will store a single JSON blob under the key `"polyglot-data"` and implement every method above by reading/writing that blob. All methods are async (returning Promises) even though localStorage is synchronous -- this ensures a future database provider (e.g., IndexedDB, Supabase, Prisma) slots in without changing call sites.

The factory in `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/lib/storage/index.ts`:

```typescript
import type { StorageProvider } from "./interface";
import { LocalStorageProvider } from "./local-storage";

let instance: StorageProvider | null = null;

export function getStorage(): StorageProvider {
  if (!instance) {
    instance = new LocalStorageProvider();
  }
  return instance;
}

export type { StorageProvider };
```

To switch to a database later, you change only this factory function and add a new implementation file -- zero changes to any component or context.

## 4. SM-2 Algorithm

In `/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/lib/sm2.ts`:

```typescript
import type { FlashcardProgress, SM2Rating } from "@/types";

export function calculateSM2(
  current: FlashcardProgress,
  rating: SM2Rating
): FlashcardProgress {
  let { easeFactor, interval, repetitions } = current;

  if (rating < 3) {
    // Failed: reset repetitions, keep ease factor
    repetitions = 0;
    interval = 1;
  } else {
    // Success
    if (repetitions === 0) {
      interval = 1;
    } else if (repetitions === 1) {
      interval = 6;
    } else {
      interval = Math.round(interval * easeFactor);
    }
    repetitions += 1;
  }

  // Update ease factor (minimum 1.3)
  easeFactor = Math.max(
    1.3,
    easeFactor + (0.1 - (5 - rating) * (0.08 + (5 - rating) * 0.02))
  );

  const now = new Date();
  const nextReview = new Date(now);
  nextReview.setDate(nextReview.getDate() + interval);

  return {
    ...current,
    easeFactor,
    interval,
    repetitions,
    lastReviewDate: now.toISOString(),
    nextReviewDate: nextReview.toISOString(),
  };
}

export function createInitialProgress(
  vocabularyId: string,
  languageCode: string
): FlashcardProgress {
  return {
    vocabularyId,
    languageCode: languageCode as any,
    easeFactor: 2.5,
    interval: 0,
    repetitions: 0,
    nextReviewDate: new Date().toISOString(),
    lastReviewDate: new Date().toISOString(),
  };
}

export function isDue(progress: FlashcardProgress): boolean {
  return new Date(progress.nextReviewDate) <= new Date();
}
```

## 5. Content Data Files

Language content is defined as TypeScript modules (not JSON) so we get type checking, autocompletion, and can use expressions. Example structure for Japanese (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/data/japanese/vocabulary.ts`):

```typescript
import type { VocabularyEntry } from "@/types";

export const japaneseVocabulary: VocabularyEntry[] = [
  {
    id: "ja-vocab-001",
    languageCode: "ja",
    term: "こんにちは",
    reading: "konnichiwa",
    definition: "Hello",
    exampleSentence: "こんにちは、元気ですか？",
    audioHint: "kohn-nee-chee-wah",
    tags: ["greetings", "beginner"],
  },
  {
    id: "ja-vocab-002",
    languageCode: "ja",
    term: "ありがとう",
    reading: "arigatou",
    definition: "Thank you",
    audioHint: "ah-ree-gah-toh",
    tags: ["greetings", "beginner"],
  },
  // ... 15-20 entries per language for seed data
];
```

Each language has parallel files. The language registry (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/data/languages.ts`) ties them together:

```typescript
import type { Language, VocabularyEntry, Lesson, Quiz, LanguageCode } from "@/types";
import { japaneseVocabulary } from "./japanese/vocabulary";
import { japaneseLessons } from "./japanese/lessons";
import { japaneseQuizzes } from "./japanese/quizzes";
// ... spanish, french imports

export const languages: Language[] = [
  { code: "ja", name: "Japanese", nativeName: "日本語", flag: "🇯🇵" },
  { code: "es", name: "Spanish", nativeName: "Español", flag: "🇪🇸" },
  { code: "fr", name: "French", nativeName: "Français", flag: "🇫🇷" },
];

const contentMap: Record<LanguageCode, {
  vocabulary: VocabularyEntry[];
  lessons: Lesson[];
  quizzes: Quiz[];
}> = {
  ja: { vocabulary: japaneseVocabulary, lessons: japaneseLessons, quizzes: japaneseQuizzes },
  es: { vocabulary: spanishVocabulary, lessons: spanishLessons, quizzes: spanishQuizzes },
  fr: { vocabulary: frenchVocabulary, lessons: frenchLessons, quizzes: frenchQuizzes },
};

export function getLanguageContent(code: LanguageCode) {
  return contentMap[code];
}

export function getLanguage(code: LanguageCode) {
  return languages.find(l => l.code === code)!;
}
```

## 6. State Management -- React Context

Two contexts, both lean. No external state library needed -- the data is modest and React 19 context performance is sufficient.

**AppContext** (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/contexts/app-context.tsx`):

Holds: `UserProfile | null`, `selectedLanguage`, `isOnboarded`, and the storage instance. Provides actions: `selectLanguage()`, `completeLesson()`, `saveQuizAttempt()`. On mount, reads from storage. On state change, writes to storage.

**FlashcardContext** (`/Users/chiu.fyi/work/polyglot/src/contexts/flashcard-context.tsx`):

Holds: the current flashcard session state (queue of due cards, current card index, session stats). Provides actions: `rateCard(rating)`, `startSession()`, `getNextCard()`. Uses SM-2 internally and persists via the storage provider.

Both contexts are `"use client"` components wrapping the app in `layout.tsx`.

## 7. Page Routes and Component Hierarchy

### Route Structure

| Route | Purpose | Key Components |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Root redirect | Checks onboarding status, redirects to `/onboarding` or `/dashboard` |
| `/onboarding` | Language selection | `LanguageSelector` |
| `/dashboard` | Progress overview | `ProgressSummary`, `LanguageSelector` (switcher) |
| `/flashcards` | Spaced repetition study | `Flashcard`, `FlashcardControls`, `FlashcardStats` |
| `/lessons` | Lesson list | `LessonCard` list |
| `/lessons/[lessonId]` | Lesson content | `VocabularyTable`, `GrammarBlock`, link to quiz |
| `/quizzes/[quizId]` | Quiz session | `QuizQuestion`, `MultipleChoice`, `FillInBlank`, `Translation`, `QuizResults` |
| `/conversation` | AI chat | `MessageBubble`, `ConversationInput` |
| `/api/conversation` | AI API route | Server-side route handler |

### Component Hierarchy

```
RootLayout (server component)
  globals.css, Geist fonts, metadata
  AppProvider (client)
    AppShell (client)
      Sidebar (desktop) / MobileNav (mobile)
      <children> -- page content
```

Each page file (`app/dashboard/page.tsx`, etc.) is a thin server component wrapper that renders the corresponding client component from `components/`. This keeps route files small and logic in components.

```
app/dashboard/page.tsx (server)
  -> DashboardPage (client component from components/dashboard/)
       ProgressSummary
       LanguageSelector (compact switcher mode)
       Quick-action cards (Study Flashcards, Continue Lessons, etc.)
```

### Navigation

The `AppShell` component renders:
- On desktop (md+ breakpoint): a left sidebar with icon+label nav links
- On mobile: a bottom tab bar with icons

Nav items: Dashboard, Flashcards, Lessons, Quizzes, Conversation.

## 8. UI Design Approach

### Theme Extension in `globals.css`

Extend the existing Tailwind v4 theme with Polyglot-specific design tokens:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";

